      "finite_assessment": {
        "complete_old_expression_basis": "One complete independently old font-introduction prayer supplies the entire invocation and ordered new-peoples/font/adoption/humble-ministry/divine-effect petition. The only prayer-body deletion relative to the official2014comparison is the repeated mysteriis, adesto phrase; the independently old short conclusion is a separately controlled formula. The old full unit is retained without deletion; no independently old exact shortened whole Latin unit is claimed.",
        "exact_changes": [
          "Omit the contiguous old words mysteriis, adesto, leaving the old invocation adesto magnae pietatis tuae sacramentis with one invitation to presence instead of the repeated one.",
          "Replace the actually printed full old long Per Dominum conclusion with the independently old full short Per Christum conclusion and distinct response.",
          "The secondarydigital2002AP218 reads mysterio in place of ministerio. The acquired official Vatican2014VigilAP28/printed55 reads ministerio, matching the complete1922donor. This proposal explicitly follows that official2014 comparison; it does not silently emend the2002witness or authenticate2008."
        ],
        "translation_notes": "Recreandos receives new birth, preserving its regenerative force rather than amusement. Plural populos remains peoples. Parturit remains the font bearing them for God. Ministerium is ministry according to the actual official2014reading, not the different2002mysterio. The final contrast retains human humble action and divine effective power.",
        "strongest_contrary_argument": "Removing the first of two linked invocation nouns and a repeated imperative creates a real shortened arrangement, and replacing the long conclusion changes the full expression. Those changes cannot be cleared merely because all remaining words are old. The finite assessment concerns this exact old prayer with one repetitive invocation contraction and a separately old standard ending, while the complete old petition, source context and disputed modern reading remain visible.",
        "source_appointment_relation": "Old font-introduction prayer versus the official2014EasterVigil prayer after the litany. The latter is the modern comparison for this study owner; no exact2008Missal or approvedEnglish identity is inferred."
      }
