      "finite_assessment": {
        "complete_old_expression_basis": "The complete old fire blessing supplies the same whole invocation, gift of divine radiance through the Son, blessing of this new fire, heavenly-desire petition and final everlasting-feast petition in the same sequence. Three specifically enumerated omissions remove two explanatory appositions and an anaphoric conclusion qualifier; no new petition or image is supplied. This is a finite adapted-study proposal, not an unchanged old Latin body.",
        "exact_changes": [
          "Omit angularem scilicet lapidem after Filium tuum, removing the explicit cornerstone apposition.",
          "Omit productum e silice, nostris profuturum usibus before novum hunc ignem, removing the physical flint-origin and practical-use descriptions.",
          "Omit eumdem in the old full short conclusion; the complete exact Per Christum Dominum nostrum and response are separately attested in PustetAP776.",
          "Normalize coelestibus to caelestibus, capitalization, ligatures, accents and punctuation; the cross is an action marker, not an English word."
        ],
        "translation_notes": "Claritas is consistently radiance. The same fire, faithful recipients, heavenly desires, paschal feasts, pure minds and ultimate feasts all remain. The omitted cornerstone/flint/use qualifiers are not reintroduced. The two linked ut/ita petitions are retained without replacing the feasts with a generic destination.",
        "strongest_contrary_argument": "The editor deliberately removes a Christological cornerstone image and the material origin/use clauses; this changes the complete expression and could be an editorial adaptation despite adding no new words. A generic omission exemption would be invalid. The proposed individual assessment relies on a complete old prayer whose two governing petitions and ordered imagery remain intact after removal of bounded explanatory modifiers.",
        "source_appointment_relation": "Old HolySaturday new-fire blessing versus official2014Vigil new-fire blessing; complete local units and endings are compared. The separate second and third1862fire prayers are not combined with the first."
      }
    }
  ],
